  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Development of Media</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Information is a public good, and independent media nourishes democracy precisely by keeping citizens informed, raising their knowledge about public affairs, brokering dialogue and helping them understand each other. Impartially informed and knowledgeable citizens can actively participate in democracy and make informed decisions. Media pluralism provides choice to the public. It is enabled by having a mix of public, private and community media, and offering a wide range of platforms (print, radio, TV and online) to avoid media concentration, which could restrict diversity of opinions and viewpoints in circulation. In this framework, MDE helps Member States ensure a diverse media landscape.</narrative>
  </description>
